speechtext:
that the house go into committee to consider the following resolution:
That it is expedient to introduce a measure to provide for the constitution of the corporation to

be known as the Northern Ontario Pipe Line Crown Corporation for the purposes, inter alia, of constructing, maintaining and operating a natural gas pipe line between the Ontario-Manitoba border and Kapuskasing, Ontario and of leasing, with an option to purchase, the said natural gas pipe line to the Trans-Canada Pipe Lines Limited and carrying out such leases, including the disposal by the corporation of the said pipe line in connection with such purchase option;
To provide also that the corporation may do such things as are conducive to the attainment of these purposes, that it may borrow money, the aggregate of the amounts borrowed by the corporation and outstanding at any time and the aggregate of the amounts loaned by the Minister of Finance and outstanding at any time not to exceed one hundred and thirty million dollars;
To provide further for the appointment and remuneration of directors, officers and employees incidental to the administration of the act.
